TEXT 0 560 Left 2 ;WHAT CHANGED IN THIS FILE, AND WHY\nCab: was 621u -> NOW 0.621u. The box is 88 L: Cab = V/(rho*c^2) = 0.621e-6, so 621u was 1000 times too big and the box did nothing in the circuit.\n      The old Cms = 0.35 mm/N hid this: it had the box spring mixed into the driver (1.012 and 0.509 mm/N in series). The box now sits where it belongs, in Cab.\nRal: was 11818.8 -> REMOVED. That number is rho*c/Sd, which is not a leak. Measured peak is 121 ohm, so this sealed box has almost no leak.\nMab: was a 0 H inductor with Rser=1p -> NOW a plain wire. LTspice gives wrong answers with that combination (vented peaks came out 13 and 15 ohm instead of 31 and 50).\nMmd: was 39.94 g -> NOW 36.19 g. The 39.94 g from the free-air measurement already includes the air on the cone, and Ma1f (3.75 g) adds that air again.\n      So Mmd = 39.94 g - 3.75 g, and the total stays 39.94 g.\nCms: NOW 1.229 mm/N in every file. This is the rubber suspension of the driver only, from extract_ltspice.m. The driver is the same in all three boxes, so these values never change.\nRESULT: 42.1 Hz / 116 ohm. Measured (labD_woofer_closed): 41.8 Hz / 121 ohm. To see it: plot 1/I(Vd1).
